<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">prone</ansi>

<ansi fg="red">Prone</ansi> is a combat condition that occurs when you've been knocked to the ground by
special attacks like <ansi fg="command">bash</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">trip</ansi>, or <ansi fg="command">kick</ansi>.

<ansi fg="yellow">How to Become Prone:</ansi>

  - Hit by a successful <ansi fg="command">bash</ansi> attack (40% base knockdown chance)
  - Hit by a successful <ansi fg="command">trip</ansi> attack (60% base knockdown chance)
  - Hit by a successful <ansi fg="command">kick</ansi> attack (35% base knockdown chance)

  Knockdown chances are modified by opposed skill checks (attacker vs defender).

<ansi fg="yellow">Effects While Prone:</ansi>

  <ansi fg="red">Attack Penalties:</ansi>
    - -30 to attack success (harder to fight from the ground)
    - -20% damage dealt (less power behind attacks)

  <ansi fg="red">Defense Penalties:</ansi>
    - -50% dodge effectiveness (can't move to avoid)
    - -30% parry effectiveness (compromised stance)
    - -20% block effectiveness (shield still works somewhat)

  <ansi fg="red">Vulnerability:</ansi>
    - Attackers get +20 to hit you (easy target on the ground)

  <ansi fg="red">Restrictions:</ansi>
    - Cannot flee from combat
    - Cannot move to other rooms

<ansi fg="yellow">Recovery:</ansi>

You have two ways to recover from being prone:

  1. <ansi fg="stat">Automatic Recovery:</ansi>
     - After 1 full round minimum, you automatically attempt to stand each round
     - Success chance based on Dexterity (25 DEX = 25%, 100 DEX = 53%, 300 DEX = 75%)
     - Costs your first action that round (only 1 attack while attempting)
     - No stamina cost

  2. <ansi fg="stat">Manual Recovery:</ansi> (<ansi fg="command">help stand</ansi>)
     - Use <ansi fg="command">stand</ansi> command for guaranteed success
     - Costs 15% of maximum stamina
     - Requires at least 15% stamina remaining
     - Still uses your action for that round

<ansi fg="yellow">Strategy:</ansi>

Being prone is dangerous! Your opponent gets significant advantages. However, automatic
recovery is free (just costs your action), so save stamina unless you MUST stand
immediately. High Dexterity characters recover faster.

